    Suggested Action Items: Pre-defined tag selections (e.g., "Schedule parent call", "Assign remedial worksheet", "Monitor peer interactions").

4. Implementation Roadmap (Sprint 1 to MVP)
Step 1: Database Setup & RLS (Supabase)

Initialize a free Supabase project.

Configure Row-Level Security (RLS) policies so teachers can only read and write data for their assigned classes and students.

Step 2: Rapid Data Entry UI

Build the Daily Class Grid (/classes/[id]/daily) using a compact tabular format with keyboard-friendly inputs (e.g., Space to toggle submission status, 1-click badge to drop a flag).

Ensure end-of-day logging takes less than 60–90 seconds per class.

Step 3: The End-of-Day Attention QueueBuild /dashboard/attention-queue using the deterministic scoring query.Render cards categorized by urgency:Red (High Priority): $\ge 2$ consecutive missing assignments or active high-severity behavioral/academic flags.Amber (Medium Priority): Single missing assignment or minor concept struggle.

Step 4: Printable / Exportable PTM SheetUse standard browser print CSS (@media print) on the /students/[id]/ptm route so teachers can generate a clean 1-page PDF report for parents with zero paid document-export services.
]